REST API Kya Hai?

REST ka matlab hai Representational State Transfer — ye ek architecture style hai jo web services banane ke liye use hota hai.
REST API ka kaam hota hai client (browser, mobile app) aur server ke beech me data exchange karna, mostly HTTP protocol use karke.

1. REST API ke Principles

Stateless – Har request independent hoti hai, server previous request ka data ya state yaad nahi rakhta.

Client-Server – Client UI handle kare, server data/business logic handle kare.

Uniform Interface – Standard way of communication (URLs, methods, responses).

Cacheable – Responses cache kiye ja sakte hain performance improve karne ke liye.

2. REST me Common HTTP Methods
| Method | Kaam (Roman Urdu)                 |
| ------ | --------------------------------- |
| GET    | Data read/retrieve karna          |
| POST   | Naya data create karna            |
| PUT    | Data update karna (poora replace) |
| PATCH  | Data update karna (partially)     |
| DELETE | Data delete karna                 |

3. Example URL Structure
GET    /api/users           → sab users ka data
GET    /api/users/5         → sirf user id 5 ka data
POST   /api/users           → naya user create
PUT    /api/users/5         → user id 5 update
DELETE /api/users/5         → user id 5 delete

4. REST API ka Data Format

Mostly JSON ya XML hota hai.
Example JSON Response:

{
  "id": 5,
  "name": "Talha",
  "email": "talha@example.com"
}

5. REST API ke Advantages

Simple aur easy to understand

Language independent (Java, Python, JS sab use kar sakte hain)

Scalability aur flexibility zyada hoti hai